00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.630
What the joke is that he's an idiot.
这个笑话的精髓就在于他是个白痴。

314
00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.630
Yes, that's the joke about him.
没错，关于他的笑话就是这个。

315
00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:08.110
That is the joke.
这确实是个笑话。

316
00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:12.270
I found myself hoping it didn't offend anyone this many years later
我当时心想，时隔这么多年，希望这没有冒犯到任何人

317
00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:18.270
because it's about him just being an idiot about food and they're being actual important distinctions.
因为这只是讲他在食物方面是个白痴，而那些其实是很重要的区别。

318
00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:21.070
And he's just, Barney is from Staten Island.
而且他这个人嘛，巴尼来自斯塔滕岛。

319
00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:24.030
You know, Barney's a guy who grew up on Staten Island really poor.
你知道的，巴尼是个在斯塔滕岛长大、家境非常贫寒的人。

320
00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:28.190
And he just, there are moments where Barney, he's putting on all the sophistication and suits and
他只是，有时候巴尼会刻意表现得很成熟、穿着西装、

321
00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:29.390
scotches and cigars.
喝着苏格兰威士忌、抽着雪茄。

322
00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:33.310
But I think in the end, he doesn't know stuff.
但我认为归根结底，他其实孤陋寡闻。

323
00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:35.150
Well, you know, he doesn't know world cuisine.
嗯，你知道的，他根本不懂世界各地的好吃的。

324
00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:37.870
He's not actually as fancy as that suit suggests.
他其实并没有他那身西装看起来那么高档。

325
00:13:38.350 --> 00:13:40.030
That's, I think what's behind that.
我觉得，这才是那些笑话背后的含义。

326
00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:43.470
Well, I do think he knows the best cigars and he knows the best suits.
不过，我觉得他确实懂最好的雪茄，也懂最好的西装。

327
00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.310
He's chosen his area of expertise.
他选择了自己的专长领域。

328
00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:46.350
Right, right.
对的，对的。

329
00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:50.350
But he doesn't, he hasn't actually been like worldly and educated.
但他并没有，他其实并没有那么见多识广、受过良好教育。

330
00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.910
You know, he hasn't, that's not really who he is.
你知道的，他没那水平，那并不是真正的他。

331
00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.270
And I think that's where that joke's coming from.
我想那个笑话的出发点就在这里。

332
00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.310
But I hope it wasn't.
但我希望事实并非如此。

333
00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:59.870
I hope people don't watch a joke and feel like it was being glib about those things he's talking about.
我希望人们在看这个笑话时，不会觉得它对巴尼提到的那些东西表现得过于轻率。

334
00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.630
It's supposed to be a joke about Barney.
这本来应该是一个关于巴尼的笑话。

335
00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.030
But I did, I found myself wondering for two seconds about it.
不过我的确有那么两秒钟在琢磨这件事。

336
00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:09.550
It's a tricky thing when writers want to write a character that is less than evolved.
当编剧想要塑造一个思想不够成熟的角色时，这是一件很棘手的事情。

337
00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:13.870
Because it's not like every, this is something I really struggle with people think,
因为并不是每个人都……这是我经常纠结的一个问题，人们会觉得，

338
00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.710
oh, you wrote it, you must believe that.
哦，既然是你写的，那你肯定就是这么想的。

339
00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.950
It's like, no, that's not true.
这就好比，不对，根本不是那回事。

340
00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:22.590
I'm writing a character that believes that and I do not endorse that in any way.
我塑造的只是一个有这种想法的角色，我本人绝对不赞同这种观点。

341
00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.110
Yeah, that's very frustrating.
对，这真的很让人沮丧。

342
00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:27.950
Because you, because the whole idea is to write characters convincingly and get into their point
因为你，因为整个理念就是要把角色写得令人信服，并走入他们的视角

343
00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.430
of view that's different from maybe your point of view.
这个视角可能与你自己的视角不同。

344
00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.710
Maybe it's entirely anathema to your point of view.
也许它完全与你的观点背道而驰。

345
00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:37.630
But you are, as a writer, your job is to say what that person might say.
但作为一名编剧，你的工作就是写出那个人可能会说的话。

346
00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:38.110
Right.
没错。

347
00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:38.910
And I really inhabit that.
而且我真的完全代入了那个角色。

348
00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.750
And an actor's job is to make that feel true.
而演员的工作就是让这种代入感显得真实。

349
00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:46.350
And yeah, it's always a little bit of a high-wire act, I would say.
是的，我觉得这总有点像是在走钢丝。

350
00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:50.190
Yeah, but we want to populate our stories.
对，但我们还是想让自己的故事里充满各种各样的角色。

351
00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:55.310
You don't want to populate your stories with people who are just perpetually virtuous.
你不会想让你的故事里充满那些永远品德高尚的人。

352
00:14:56.110 --> 00:15:00.190
There's no story, because there's no conflict when someone says there's nowhere to go.
那样就没有故事了，因为当有人说无处可去时，根本就没有冲突。

353
00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.270
There's no evolution.
没有演变。

354
00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:02.830
There's no conflict.
没有冲突。

355
00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.110
They're always making the right decision.
他们总是做出正确的决定。

356
00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:05.550
They're always saying the right thing.
他们总是说正确的话。

357
00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:09.150
No, I've thought a lot about this and we've talked about it on the podcaSt.
不，我对此思考了很多，我们在播客上也讨论过。

358
00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:12.510
And these moments come up and you go, that kind of is who Barney is.
当这些时刻出现时，你会觉得，这正是巴尼的性格所在。

359
00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:17.390
But it's not the most evolved comment, but that is kind of who he is,
虽然这不是最成熟的言论，但这确实挺符合他的性格，

360
00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.670
especially at this point in the series.
特别是在剧集的这个阶段。

361
00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.110
We're going to evolve from where we go.
我们会从我们出发的地方不断进化。

362
00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:24.430
But yeah, I mean, it's funny how I met your mother.
但说实话，这就是《老爸老妈浪漫史》有趣的地方。

363
00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:26.990
We didn't say this in last week's episode.
我们在上周的节目中没说过这个。

364
00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:31.230
But in the time we had a little bit of a break between our podcast seasons,
但在我们播客季与季之间的一小段休息时间里，

365
00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:33.230
how much of a mother turned 21 years old?
《老爸老妈浪漫史》竟然已经21岁了？

366
00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:35.310
2005.
2005年。

367
00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:36.350
We don't have it until it's gotch.
直到它能点威士忌之前，我们都不算真正拥有它。

368
00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:41.310
Oh, yeah, I did a little post that said I love a show that's old enough to order its own scotch.
哦，对，我发了一条小动态，说我喜欢一部已经老到可以合法点苏格兰威士忌的剧。

369
00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:42.990
And it's true.
确实如此。

370
00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:47.070
21 September 19th, 2005 to September 19th,
21年，从2005年9月19日到

371
00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:48.990
2026 and we hit that moment.
2026年9月19日，我们迎来了这个时刻。

372
00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.870
And I just wanted to acknowledge that.
我只是想表达一下感慨。

373
00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.350
The 21 years, it's a long time, right?
21年，这很长时间，对吧？

374
00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:56.110
Oh, there's some applause happening.
哦，现场传来了一些掌声。

375
00:15:56.670 --> 00:16:00.590
Our studio audience is getting bigger and bigger as we go.
我们的演播室观众随着节目的进行越来越多了。

376
00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:02.030
I know, it's really gotten to be ahead.
我知道，观众人数真的越来越多了。

377
00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:05.310
If you want to order tickets to come see us live, please write it.
如果你想订票来现场看我们，请写信给我们。

378
00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:08.030
It's cool.
这很酷。

379
00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.070
It's 21 years, right?
已经21年了，对吧？

380
00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.190
That's a long time.
这很长时间了。

381
00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.350
And yeah, stuff changes.
而且，事情确实会变。

382
00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:15.310
You think you rethink some things and it's just a cool.
你会重新思考一些事情，这真的很酷。

383
00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:18.670
I just want to acknowledge that moment because it's a cool moment to be looking back.
我只是想纪念那个时刻，因为回首过去是一个非常酷的时刻。

384
00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:23.470
It made me excited that we're doing the podcast to be able to hit that milestone as we're doing the podcaSt.
这让我很高兴我们正在做这个播客，能在做播客的同时迎来这个里程碑。

385
00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:25.310
And that's what this whole episode's about, right?
这也是这一整集的主题，对吧？

386
00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:28.830
This whole episode's about reflection and memory.
这一整集都是关于反思和记忆的。

387
00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:31.470
And did New York change or did you change?
是纽约变了，还是你变了？

388
00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:33.070
And I think the thing at the heart of this episode,
我想这一集的核心，

389
00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:36.910
I'll give Carter Bay is a lot of credit because this is a very Carter episode,
我要给卡特·贝斯记很大功劳，因为这非常具有卡特的风格，

390
00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:37.390
I want to say.
我想这么说。

391
00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:40.030
I feel like he did a lot of brilliant work on this episode.
我觉得他在这一集里做了很多极其出色的工作。

392
00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:44.590
And I think where he was coming from with the theme of this episode was,
我想这一集主题的出发点是，

393
00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:51.310
as you get older, does your capacity for pure joy and wonder diminish?
随着年龄的增长，你对纯粹喜悦和惊叹的感受能力是否在减弱？

394
00:16:51.310 --> 00:16:53.790
So that you'll always think, no, it's not that thing.
以至于你总会觉得，不，不是那种感觉。

395
00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:58.350
I'm not finding that exact thing that felt that exact way 10 years ago,
我找不到10年前那种感觉完全一致的东西了，

396
00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.510
but really it's you who's changed.
但实际上是你自己变了。

397
00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:04.590
And it's that search for that elusive spark and it's about aging.
这正是对那种难以捉摸的火花的寻找，也是关于变老的思考。

398
00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:08.910
And it comes from this place where even as we were doing this show and we're in season four here,
它源于这样一种情况：甚至在我们制作这部剧、也就是第四季的时候，

399
00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.950
we would go back and visit New York, Carter and I would, right?
我和卡特还会回去重访纽约，对吧？

400
00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:14.270
My whole family was still there, Carter and people there.
我的整个家庭都还在那里，卡特和那里的其他人也是。

401
00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:15.710
And we would go back and visit New York.
我们会回去造访纽约。

402
00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:23.310
And one by one, Josh, we would see all of these really important landmarks of our 20s
乔希，我们会眼睁睁看着那些对我们二十多岁时至关重要的地标，

403
00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:24.590
in New York disappear.
在纽约一个接一个地消失。

404
00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:30.510
So that little montage in this episode where Future Ted, name checks, three places in New York,
所以在这一集里的那个小剪辑中，未来泰德点名了纽约的三个地方，

405
00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:33.310
three places he name checks is the elbow room.
他点名的三个地方之一就是 Elbow Room 酒吧。

406
00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:36.750
That's where our band, the solids used to play concerts in the village.
那是我们的乐队 The Solids 以前在村里举办音乐会的地方。

407
00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:40.750
The Fez on the upper side of her car.
上城区的 Fez 俱乐部。

408
00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:42.270
She shows it Fez when I was at NYU.
我上纽约大学时她带我去过 Fez。

409
00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:45.630
Carter and I used to go with a couple of our great late show friends,
我和卡特以前经常和几个《深夜秀》的好友一起去，

410
00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:46.510
late show writer friends.
《深夜秀》的编剧朋友。

411
00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:47.710
We'd go up there to Fez.
我们会去那里的 Fez。

412
00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.830
We would walk in, they knew what songs we like, they're the DJ there.
我们走进去，那里的 DJ 知道我们喜欢什么歌。

413
00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:55.070
The DJ there, Josh was named, and I don't know if I've ever told you this.
那里的 DJ 叫什么名字，乔希，我不知道我有没有跟你说过这个。

414
00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:55.710
Oh, no, I know this.
噢，不，我知道这个。

415
00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:56.510
You know this.
你知道这个。

416
00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.790
Josh Mosby.
乔希·莫斯比（Josh Mosby）。

417
00:17:57.790 --> 00:17:58.590
Josh Mosby.
乔希·莫斯比。

418
00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:03.550
So the DJ at Fez had a last name Mosby and we thought it was cool.
所以 Fez 的 DJ 姓莫斯比，我们觉得这很酷。

419
00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:06.670
And we would walk in and he had our band CD, the solids,
我们走进去时，他有我们乐队 The Solids 的 CD，

420
00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:09.390
the solids who were playing at the elbow room at that point.
当时 The Solids 正在 Elbow Room 演出。

421
00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:14.110
And he would watch us walk in, wave to us and put on our music, playing in Fez.
他看着我们走进来，向我们挥手，然后放起我们的音乐，在 Fez 播放。

422
00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:16.510
And we were like, God damn, I love this guy, Josh Mosby.
我们当时想，天哪，我太喜欢这家伙了，乔希·莫斯比。

423
00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.270
He's rocking our single solids.
他在放我们乐队的单曲。

424
00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:20.750
And he played other songs he knew that we like because he just got to be friendly.
他还播放了他知道我们喜欢的其他歌曲，因为大家渐渐成了朋友。

425
00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:23.470
And Mosby stuck in our head.
而莫斯比这个名字就留在了我们的脑海里。

426
00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:25.550
And Fez, the elbow room is gone.
还有 Fez，Elbow Room，现在都消失了。

427
00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:27.150
The elbow room did become a bank.
Elbow Room 后来确实变成了一家银行。

428
00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:29.550
Carter used to live right above the elbow room.
卡特以前就住在 Elbow Room 楼上。

429
00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:30.590
And we used to play concert show.
我们以前经常去演出。

430
00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:34.830
We'd take his amp down from his apartment and just take it into the elbow room.
我们会把他的音箱从公寓搬下来，直接搬进 Elbow Room。

431
00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:37.630
And we'd play the show and that's gone.
然后我们去演出，而那个地方现在已经没了。

432
00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.710
Josh Mosby is probably out there going,
乔希·莫斯比现在大概在想，

433
00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:42.190
wow, there's a lot of dogs named Mosby.
哇，怎么有这么多叫莫斯比的狗。

434
00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:44.910
Yeah, by the way, Josh Mosby, if you're hearing this, reach out.
是的，顺便说一句，乔希·莫斯比，如果你听到这个，联系我们吧。

435
00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:49.310
We don't know what became a Josh Mosby, but his name lives on.
我们不知道乔希·莫斯比后来怎么样了，但他的名字流传了下来。

436
00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.510
And McCall's was a great Irish bar that Carter and I would go to
McCall's 是一家很棒的爱尔兰酒吧，1996 年夏天我们在 MTV 实习时，

437
00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:57.150
when we were interns at MTV in the summer of 1996 because
我和卡特经常去那里，因为

438
00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:01.150
McCall's was like a block or so away from like 1697 broad.
McCall's 离百老汇 1697 号只有大概一个街区左右。

439
00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:02.190
No, am I saying that right?
不对，我没说错吧？

440
00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:08.030
A 1697 broadway is either late Joe or maybe 1515.
百老汇 1697 号要么是《深夜秀》的地址，或者是 1515 号。

441
00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:10.590
Somewhere on broadway was the MTV headquarters and it was
百老汇的某个地方是 MTV 总部，而

442
00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:11.390
McCall's is right there.
McCall's 就在那附近。

443
00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:15.310
We go there and one by one, we watch all those places become
我们去那里，然后眼睁睁地看着所有这些地方一个接一个地变成

444
00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:18.910
essentially Goliath National Bank or a pharmacy.
实质上的歌利亚国家银行（Goliath National Bank）或药店。

445
00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:20.430
Like his winery hit or a rated.
就像他的酒庄遭遇的一样。

446
00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:24.910
Well, it's also, I mean, this is getting into larger themes
嗯，这也，我是说，这涉及到了本集的更大主题，

447
00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.990
of this episode, which is like on its surface,
表面上看，

448
00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:28.910
the search for the best burger in New York.
是在纽约寻找最好的汉堡。

449
00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:33.550
But it's really a big question about time and how time changes us.
但它实际上探讨的是关于时间以及时间如何改变我们的宏大问题。

450
00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:36.110
How time changes the city, how time changes us.
时间如何改变这座城市，时间又如何改变我们。

451
00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.710
