you know, she's about, I don't know, she's about my age, right?
你知道的，她大概，我不知道，她大概和我差不多大，对吧？

609
00:25:22.590 --> 00:25:26.590
But one of her things was she loved it so much.
但她的其中一个感悟是她太喜欢了。

610
00:25:27.390 --> 00:25:32.030
And it reminded her how hard it is to love something
这让她想起去疯狂热爱某样东西有多难，

611
00:25:32.030 --> 00:25:34.190
that much the way you love something in your youth.
就像你在年轻时爱上某样东西那样。

612
00:25:34.190 --> 00:25:36.590
Because when you meet, it's kind of like the line in,
因为当你相遇时，有点像那句台词，

613
00:25:36.590 --> 00:25:38.030
I think before sunset,
我想是在《爱在日落黄昏时》里，

614
00:25:38.030 --> 00:25:40.350
when you're young and you meet people and you fall in love,
当你年轻时遇到某人并坠入爱河，

615
00:25:40.350 --> 00:25:42.990
you just assume you're going to keep meeting people and falling in love.
你会理所当然地觉得你会不断遇到新人并坠入爱河。

616
00:25:42.990 --> 00:25:47.150
You assume there's a limitless supply of people you're going to connect with
你以为你会遇到无穷无尽的人，能够与他们产生心灵的共鸣，

617
00:25:47.150 --> 00:25:50.110
in walking around Europe or wherever you meet people.
无论是在欧洲漫步还是在任何你遇到人的地方。

618
00:25:50.110 --> 00:25:54.990
And the same way you think I'm going to keep falling in love with works of art,
就像你觉得我会不断爱上各种艺术作品一样，

619
00:25:54.990 --> 00:25:58.430
the way I did when I was 16 or 19 or 21.
就像我16岁、19岁或21岁时那样。

620
00:25:58.430 --> 00:26:03.470
And the truth is that sometimes you are at such a space in your life
而事实是，有时你正处于人生中的某个阶段，

621
00:26:03.470 --> 00:26:08.030
where your heart is open to beauty or greatness.
你的心灵对美或伟大敞开着。

622
00:26:08.670 --> 00:26:11.310
In a way that like, it doesn't always,
以至于它并不总是……

623
00:26:11.310 --> 00:26:14.510
the universe doesn't reliably deliver that your whole life.
宇宙并不会在你的一生中稳定地带来那种体验。

624
00:26:14.510 --> 00:26:18.830
And I think she had this crisis moment that was inspired by this thing that she loved
我想她经历了一次危机时刻，是由她喜爱的事物所激发出来的

625
00:26:18.830 --> 00:26:24.590
because she realized that was the passion with which she loved it almost felt youthful to her.
因为她意识到那种炽热的爱对她来说几乎有一种青春的气息。

626
00:26:24.590 --> 00:26:25.150
Yeah.
是的。

627
00:26:25.150 --> 00:26:27.630
And she realized how rare that kind of thing is.
她意识到那种东西是多么罕见。

628
00:26:28.350 --> 00:26:29.310
It's so rare.
实在是太罕见了。

629
00:26:29.310 --> 00:26:37.950
And I suspect that's part of why us humans keep having kids is just we lose that
我猜这也是为什么我们人类不断生孩子的部分原因，因为我们失去了那种感觉，

630
00:26:37.950 --> 00:26:42.430
and we want to see our children experience it and just be near it.
我们想看到我们的孩子去体验它，并离它近一点。

631
00:26:42.430 --> 00:26:46.750
We need some external force to reacquaint us with wonder.
我们需要某种外在的力量来让我们重新找回惊叹的感觉。

632
00:26:46.750 --> 00:26:47.230
Yeah.
对。

633
00:26:47.230 --> 00:26:49.230
Just be adjacent to that feeling,
只要能靠近那种感觉，

634
00:26:49.230 --> 00:26:51.230
even if we can't fully have it ourselves.
哪怕我们自己无法完全拥有它。

635
00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:53.950
And then every once in a while, something surprises you and gives you that feeling
然后偶尔会有什么东西给你带来惊喜，让你重新感受到那种心动，

636
00:26:53.950 --> 00:26:55.470
and you're like, why can't I have this going on?
你会想，为什么我不能一直拥有这种状态呢？

637
00:26:55.470 --> 00:26:57.070
Well, the children themselves give you that feeling.
嗯，孩子们本身就能给你这种感觉。

638
00:26:57.070 --> 00:26:58.590
The children are that feeling.
孩子们就是那种感觉。

639
00:26:58.590 --> 00:26:59.012
Right.
对的。

640
00:26:59.012 --> 00:27:00.350
That's the feeling.
那就是那种感觉。

641
00:27:00.350 --> 00:27:00.750
Yeah.
对。

642
00:27:00.750 --> 00:27:02.430
That's what adult life.
这就是成年人的生活。

643
00:27:02.430 --> 00:27:05.950
If you're lucky enough to have kids and you get to experience that wonder,
如果你足够幸运能有孩子，并且能体验到那种惊叹，

644
00:27:05.950 --> 00:27:07.950
you get a little bit of that feeling, but it's different.
你会稍微感受到一点那种感觉，但它是不一样的。

645
00:27:07.950 --> 00:27:11.150
And Marshall is longing for innocence.
而马歇尔渴望的是纯真。

646
00:27:11.150 --> 00:27:14.910
That's why I like that the Galat National Bank thing happens in this episode
这就是为什么我喜欢这一集里出现加拉特国民银行这事儿，

647
00:27:14.910 --> 00:27:19.550
because it is about that was the version of me that was going to be somebody else.
因为它关乎到，那曾是我原本可能成为另一个人时的版本。

648
00:27:19.550 --> 00:27:23.710
That was the version of me that was going to go a different direction than I'm now having to go
那曾是我原本要走向不同方向的版本，而我现在不得不接受现实，

649
00:27:23.710 --> 00:27:25.150
because I'm unemployed.
因为我失业了。

650
00:27:25.150 --> 00:27:26.510
I'm not wearing pants.
我甚至都没穿裤子。

651
00:27:26.510 --> 00:27:28.190
I do want to start a family one day.
我确实想在某一天组建一个家庭。

652
00:27:28.750 --> 00:27:31.630
And life is showing me that it's about compromises.
生活也让我明白，生活就是妥协。

653
00:27:31.630 --> 00:27:35.230
And it's not about magic nights where you stumble upon something
它不是那种让你偶然遇见的魔幻夜晚，

654
00:27:35.230 --> 00:27:36.430
euphoric all the time.
时刻都充满着狂喜。

655
00:27:36.430 --> 00:27:38.110
It's about reality.
它关乎现实。

656
00:27:38.110 --> 00:27:41.150
And it's impossible to be as an adult.
而且作为一个成年人，这是不可能做到的。

657
00:27:41.150 --> 00:27:44.510
And this is a sad thing for young people to hear and realize
年轻人听到并意识到这一点其实挺让人难过的，

658
00:27:45.230 --> 00:27:48.750
a hundred percent purity is kind of like impossible.
百分之百的纯粹几乎是不可能的。

659
00:27:49.310 --> 00:27:49.790
It's true.
确实如此。

660
00:27:51.710 --> 00:27:52.590
It's really hard.
这真的很艰难。

661
00:27:52.590 --> 00:27:53.150
It's really hard.
这真的很艰难。

662
00:27:53.150 --> 00:27:54.590
It's a hard thing to accept.
这是一件很难接受的事情。

663
00:27:54.590 --> 00:27:56.350
It's a hard thing to accept.
这是一件很难接受的事情。

664
00:27:56.430 --> 00:28:00.830
You get little moments of it where you like brush past that feeling and the crowd kind of thing.
你偶尔会体验到短暂的时刻，比如那种擦肩而过的感觉，以及人群带来的那种氛围。

665
00:28:00.830 --> 00:28:03.790
But it's not quite the same.
但又完全不是那么回事。

666
00:28:03.790 --> 00:28:07.390
And I think that's what sparks the idea for this episode is Carter.
我想这就是这集节目的灵感来源，也就是卡特。

667
00:28:07.390 --> 00:28:09.230
Carter is a very nostalgic guy.
卡特是一个非常怀旧的人。

668
00:28:09.230 --> 00:28:11.390
He's a very romantic guy.
他是一个非常浪漫的人。

669
00:28:12.350 --> 00:28:14.910
He would go back to New York and he'd be the kind of guy that's like,
他会回到纽约，然后会是那种会说……的人，

670
00:28:14.910 --> 00:28:16.270
let's go check out the elbow room.
我们去看看Elbow Room酒吧吧。

671
00:28:16.270 --> 00:28:19.230
I remember we used to play all those gigs there as the solids.
我记得我们以前作为The Solids乐队在那里演过很多场。

672
00:28:19.230 --> 00:28:21.470
And you go back and it's a fucking bank.
等你回去的时候，发现它特么变成了一家银行。

673
00:28:22.670 --> 00:28:25.150
And it's just heartbreaking.
这简直让人心碎。

674
00:28:25.150 --> 00:28:27.470
It's like, but no, my memories live in there.
就好像，不对啊，我的回忆还在里面呢。

675
00:28:28.430 --> 00:28:30.110
What happened to those memories?
那些回忆怎么不见了？

676
00:28:30.110 --> 00:28:31.310
Those memories are gone.
那些回忆都已经消失了。

677
00:28:31.310 --> 00:28:32.190
It's a bank now.
现在那里变成了一家银行。

678
00:28:32.910 --> 00:28:38.110
And it's just a devastating feeling that you start having more and more often
那种感觉非常令人心碎，而且随着你年龄的增长，

679
00:28:38.110 --> 00:28:39.070
as you get older, right?
这种感觉会越来越频繁，对吧？

680
00:28:39.070 --> 00:28:43.150
We're in our thirties at this point and are coming up in our mid thirties at this point
我们在拍《老爸老妈浪漫史》时，这时候我们已经三十多岁了，正迈向三十岁中期。

681
00:28:43.150 --> 00:28:45.310
in the run of how I met your mother.
在《老爸老妈浪漫史》的拍摄历程中。

682
00:28:45.310 --> 00:28:47.470
And those twenties, those mid twenties,
而那些二十多岁的光阴，二十多岁的中期，

683
00:28:47.470 --> 00:28:50.030
we're starting to get more and more in the rear view.
正渐渐离我们越来越远，消失在后视镜中。

684
00:28:50.030 --> 00:28:51.790
And those landmark plays.
还有那些标志性的地方。

685
00:28:51.950 --> 00:28:55.870
You also assume that your New York that you discovered is New York.
你还会以为你所发现的那个纽约就是真正的纽约。

686
00:28:55.870 --> 00:28:56.670
Like, that's New York.
就好像，那就是纽约。

687
00:28:56.670 --> 00:28:57.870
That's New York here to stay.
那是永恒存在的纽约。

688
00:28:57.870 --> 00:29:00.430
But you live there for decades and you're like,
但你在那里住了几十年后，你会觉得，

689
00:29:00.430 --> 00:29:01.470
this is not going to.
这一切是不会长久的。

690
00:29:01.470 --> 00:29:04.670
Do you remember, did you ever go to other music by Tower Records,
你还记得吗，你以前去过 Tower Records 旗下的另一家唱片店 Other Music 吗？

691
00:29:04.670 --> 00:29:06.670
like downtown, like fourth and Broadway?
比如市中心那家，在第四街和百老汇大道交界处？

692
00:29:06.670 --> 00:29:07.870
Yeah, I think so.
对，我想去过。

693
00:29:07.870 --> 00:29:11.150
There was this little independent record store that was actually incredible.
那里有一家很小的独立唱片店，真的很棒。

694
00:29:11.150 --> 00:29:12.110
They would do it in studio.
他们会在店里搞现场录音。

695
00:29:12.110 --> 00:29:14.430
But I discovered so much music there
我在那里发现了好多音乐，

696
00:29:15.310 --> 00:29:17.710
because they would do like staff recs and all this stuff.
因为他们会做员工推荐之类的活动。

697
00:29:17.710 --> 00:29:18.190
Yeah.
是的。

698
00:29:18.190 --> 00:29:23.550
And I was just, it was when I was really becoming like a serious music fan.
那正好是我真正成为一个严肃的音乐迷的时候。

699
00:29:24.270 --> 00:29:26.830
Other music was like the spot.
Other Music 就是这样一个地方。

700
00:29:26.830 --> 00:29:28.190
And I remember when it closed down,
我记得它关门的时候，

701
00:29:28.190 --> 00:29:31.070
I was like, that feels impossible that this place could close.
我当时就想，这个地方居然会倒闭，感觉太不可思议了。

702
00:29:31.070 --> 00:29:35.470
That was like where everyone found their great indie artists.
那可是所有人发掘优秀独立音乐的地方。

703
00:29:35.470 --> 00:29:36.430
Yeah.
对啊。

704
00:29:36.430 --> 00:29:36.750
Yeah.
没错。

705
00:29:36.750 --> 00:29:39.950
And then Tower Records, which was the GNB of music,
然后还有作为音乐界GNB的Tower Records唱片行，

706
00:29:40.910 --> 00:29:41.950
was right across the street.
就在街对面。

707
00:29:42.990 --> 00:29:45.630
And it was always this kind of weird David and Goliath thing.
那总有一种大卫与歌利亚式的奇妙对抗感。

708
00:29:46.510 --> 00:29:48.510
And now we don't even have Tower Records.
而现在我们连Tower Records都没了。

709
00:29:48.510 --> 00:29:49.310
That's a funny thing.
这挺搞笑的。

710
00:29:49.310 --> 00:29:50.510
It's like, you've got mail thing.
这就有点像电影《电子情书》里的情节。

711
00:29:50.510 --> 00:29:52.990
It's like, now we don't even have those big chain books there.
就像是，现在连那些大型连锁书店也没有了。

712
00:29:52.990 --> 00:29:54.190
Those are in trouble.
那些书店现在自身难保。

713
00:29:54.190 --> 00:29:55.070
I forgot the little ones.
我都快忘了那些小书店了。

714
00:29:55.070 --> 00:29:57.790
It's like, it is, the March of Time can be so cruel.
时光的流逝真是太残酷了。

715
00:29:58.990 --> 00:30:04.590
And this old man, he musted me, fell in love with you.
还有那个老头，他一定……爱上了你。

716
00:30:05.710 --> 00:30:07.390
New York City.
纽约市。

717
00:30:08.670 --> 00:30:10.590
And now commercials.
现在进入广告。

718
00:30:18.140 --> 00:30:20.140
End of commercials, back to show.
广告结束，回到节目。

719
00:30:21.020 --> 00:30:23.020
Well, speaking of Goliath National Bank,
对了，说到歌利亚国家银行（GNB），

720
00:30:23.020 --> 00:30:25.820
it's funny that if there is a B or C story in here,
有趣的是，如果这集里有什么B线或C线剧情的话，

721
00:30:26.380 --> 00:30:30.780
it's Barney doing these weird commercials for GNB through the episode.
那就是巴尼整集都在为GNB拍那些奇怪的广告。

722
00:30:30.780 --> 00:30:31.037
Yeah.
对啊。

723
00:30:31.037 --> 00:30:32.220
And you don't know why.
而且你一开始不知道为什么。

724
00:30:32.220 --> 00:30:33.660
Until something you do know why.
直到后来你知道了为什么。

725
00:30:33.660 --> 00:30:34.940
It has a great payoff.
有一个很棒的爆点。

726
00:30:34.940 --> 00:30:35.980
It's a great payoff, yeah.
确实是个很棒的爆点，对。

727
00:30:35.980 --> 00:30:36.780
At the end.
在最后。

728
00:30:36.780 --> 00:30:37.820
But I did notice something.
不过我确实注意到了一个细节。

729
00:30:37.820 --> 00:30:39.100
I want to give a shout out to Neil.
我想向尼尔致敬。

730
00:30:40.700 --> 00:30:43.100
Sometimes I could see when I got the C story,
有时候当我接到C线剧情时，

731
00:30:43.100 --> 00:30:44.700
like the Red Boots or something.
比如红靴子那一集什么的。

732
00:30:44.700 --> 00:30:46.620
I was dragging my boots a little bit.
我演的时候会有点懈怠。

733
00:30:47.580 --> 00:30:48.620
Neil never did.
但尼尔从来没有。

734
00:30:48.620 --> 00:30:49.500
Neil never did.
尼尔从来没有过。

735
00:30:49.500 --> 00:30:52.780
If he had a C story, he treated it like the A story.
如果他有C线剧情，他会把它当成A线剧情来演。

736
00:30:52.780 --> 00:30:53.580
Yeah.
是的。

737
00:30:53.580 --> 00:30:54.940
And that was kind of a Barney.
这很有巴尼的风格。

738
00:30:54.940 --> 00:30:56.860
Like Barney's always the main character.
就像巴尼永远是主角一样。

739
00:30:56.860 --> 00:30:57.660
Barney was always the lead.
巴尼永远是主角。

740
00:30:57.660 --> 00:31:00.940
He was the main character of the sitcom that he was living in.
他就像是生活在他自己那部情景喜剧里的主角。

741
00:31:01.500 --> 00:31:01.980
Yeah.
对啊。

742
00:31:01.980 --> 00:31:09.020
But he treated those moments of talking lovingly about Goliath National Bank
但他表现那些深情谈论歌利亚国家银行的时刻时，

743
00:31:09.020 --> 00:31:13.820
with such like funny passion and like he just needed to.
带着那种搞笑的热情，就好像他非得这么做不可。

744
00:31:13.820 --> 00:31:16.460
It was almost like he was sponsored by Goliath National Bank.
感觉他就像是被歌利亚国家银行赞助了一样。

745
00:31:16.460 --> 00:31:19.900
And he had to get them in at any moment he could.
而且他必须随时随地把广告植入进去。

746
00:31:19.900 --> 00:31:22.220
He seems crazy as he's doing them.
他在拍的时候看起来疯狂极了。

747
00:31:22.220 --> 00:31:23.820
And then at the end, you realize it's actually weird.
然后到了最后，你才发现其实这很诡异。

748
00:31:23.820 --> 00:31:26.460
The sort of suite he's trying to convince Lily
他那套说辞其实是想说服莉莉，

749
00:31:26.460 --> 00:31:27.820
that Marshall has made a good decision.
让她觉得马修做出了一个明智的决定。

750
00:31:27.820 --> 00:31:30.380
I mean, Barney's always wanting to seduce Marshall
我的意思是，巴尼总是想诱惑马修

751
00:31:30.380 --> 00:31:32.620
out of trying to save the world as environmental lawyer
从试图当个拯救世界的环保律师

752
00:31:32.620 --> 00:31:34.140
and into this corporate world.
转变成了进入这个企业世界。

753
00:31:34.140 --> 00:31:35.340
And that is a bit nefarious.
而这确实有点邪恶。

754
00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:37.900
But part of his motivation is he wants to work with Marshall.
但他的部分动机是想和马歇尔共事。

755
00:31:37.900 --> 00:31:39.340
And he was doing that for a minute.
他确实这么干了一会儿。

756
00:31:39.340 --> 00:31:40.060
Then it stopped.
然后就停了。

757
00:31:40.060 --> 00:31:42.220
Even though Marshall's not allowed on his floor.
尽管马歇尔不能去他的楼层。

758
00:31:42.220 --> 00:31:43.580
Yeah, he's still wants to write.
对，他还是想写作。

759
00:31:43.580 --> 00:31:46.060
He still wants supremacy above Marshall somehow.
他某种程度上仍然想凌驾于马歇尔之上。

760
00:31:46.060 --> 00:31:49.180
But he wants Marshall to be in his orbit because he loves Marshall
但他又想让马歇尔在自己的势力范围内，因为他喜欢马歇尔

761
00:31:49.180 --> 00:31:51.180
